From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: 3D state register writes in one inlined step (EDEN_UP_REG_WRITE_ONE_CALL, live), off by default

What: on the back (or the one GPU thread without the split), a 3D state register write (not in
execution_mask) that CallMethod's checks cannot affect (no macro collecting parameters, no write
history, no first-write trace, no profiler) writes shadow RAM, does the same-value test and sets
the dirty flags in one always-inlined step instead of CallMethod's prelude, ProcessShadowRam and a
ProcessDirtyRegisters call. The same step is used by MacroWrite's short path
(EDEN_PE_MACRO_STATE_WRITES) and by the method sink (ConsumeSinkImpl). Same registers, shadow
registers, dirty flags, deferred-draw and fast-draw-break calls. Not gated: ProcessDirtyRegisters'
body moved into an always-inlined WriteDirtyRegister that it calls (same code). The same-value rule
for the new paths is a member taken from SkipSameValueWrites() in the constructor (the draft read
the variable again; taking the old path's value means the two cannot differ).
Placed from the reviewed draft our drafts (made on T129), applied
to c68c78e without changes, plus review correction 1: in verify mode the "verifying" flag is a token
the very next CallMethod uses up, so the writes of a macro started inside a checked call are checked
one by one too.

Switches: EDEN_UP_REG_WRITE_ONE_CALL=1 (exact "1"), a live switch (Id::RegWriteOneCall, last in the
enum, ParseExactOne, not armed); off: one relaxed load and a branch per CallMethod, per MacroWrite
short-path write and per sink run, and an OR of four zero counters per sync point.
EDEN_UP_REG_WRITE_ONE_CALL_VERIFY=1 (boot, exact "1"): with the switch on, every CallMethod write
takes the old path, and each write the short path would have taken is compared with what the short
path would have left (register, shadow, write or skip and dirty flags); the first 8 differences are
logged as "Register write one call differs: ..." (HW_GPU Warning).
Log (HW_GPU Info, from ProcessSyncPoint, every 10 s once any counter moved): "Register write one
call in 10.0 s (EDEN_UP_REG_WRITE_ONE_CALL=1, _VERIFY=0): N short-path writes, N macro writes, N sink
writes, N verified, N differences (session: ...)".

Origin and credit: zortos293/Lichii 73a1b58e7d (#1095), jpkto (upstream: 260.7 instead of 278.8
instructions per 3D method), by way of waveydude/Eglantine-PS5- 711c2c7 (his core patch 0916: the
member for the same-value rule and the MacroWrite short path). Our draft v2/ports-3 and its reviews.
